\title{lwpls: Locally-Weighted Partial Least Squares for 'tidymodels'}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Locally-weighted partial least squares (LW-PLS) is a just-in-time learning method that builds a dedicated weighted partial least squares model around every new sample, where training samples are weighted by their similarity to that sample (Kim et al. (2011) \doi{10.1016/j.ijpharm.2011.10.007}). Regression (single or multiple outcomes) and classification are supported. The prediction kernel is written in C++ with 'RcppArmadillo', and the model is integrated with the 'parsnip', 'dials' and 'tune' packages so it can be used within the 'tidymodels' framework.
